{"id": "dolly-12156", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nIn music theory, what is the circle of fifths?\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The circle of fifths, also known as the chromatic scale, is a system of musical intervals that repeats every five musical degrees. It is based on the fact that a musical note can be identified by the interval between it and the note that follows it. This interval is called a \"chord\" or \"harmony,\" and it is a fundamental building block of the musical scale. In the circle of fifths, each note is located in the fifth position from the previous note, and each interval between two notes is divided into five equal parts. This system allows for a simple and easy-to-remember representation of the musical scale, and it is used in many different musical genres, from classical music to jazz and pop music.", "num_tokens": 147, "green_tokens": 84, "green_fraction": 0.5714285714285714, "z_score": 1.7320508075688774, "p_value": 0.04163225833177522, "dedup_num_tokens": 133, "dedup_green_tokens": 75, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5639097744360902, "dedup_z_score": 1.474086948191004, "dedup_p_value": 0.07022909110143055, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 48, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
