{"id": "dolly-06521", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nName three famous movies about sports.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "Certainly! Here are three classic sports movies that are widely regarded as some of the most iconic and memorable:\n1. \"Baseball: Home Run\", directed by David O. Russell and starring John Wayne and Burt Lancaster, is a classic film about a baseball team from the fictional city of Los Angeles. It tells the story of a group of players and their struggles as they navigate the challenges of the American League and the complexities of their home team.\n2. \"The Lion King\", directed by Steven Spielberg, is a beloved classic film about a group of young animals that are raised in the kingdom of Africa and are raised to be king of the animals in the kingdom. It tells the story of a family of lions who are raised to be kings and how they are affected by their family's rivalry and other issues.\n3. \"The Shawshank Redemption\", directed by Frank Darabont and starring Tim Robbins and Morgan Freeman, is a classic film about a man named Andy Dufresne who is sentenced to life in prison after being convicted of murder. He meets fellow inmate Red and their friends at the Shawshank State Penitentiary and forms an unlikely friendship as they face the harsh realities of prison life. It tells the story of a man who is held captive by the injustices of the justice system and how they affect their life and relationships.", "num_tokens": 273, "green_tokens": 145, "green_fraction": 0.5311355311355311, "z_score": 1.0288868055369642, "p_value": 0.15176643464570727, "dedup_num_tokens": 222, "dedup_green_tokens": 115, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5180180180180181, "dedup_z_score": 0.5369248441712194, "dedup_p_value": 0.29565976453295306, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 73, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-12244", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhen was the Memphis album released\n\n### Context:\nMemphis is the seventeenth album recorded by Roy Orbison, and his tenth for MGM Records. The album was released in November 1972.\n\nHistory\nThe album took three weeks to make in March and April 1972. The album had one single, \"Memphis, Tennessee\", which became a minor hit in the US, charting at #84. Also included was a new, re-recorded version of Don Gibson's \"I Can't Stop Loving You\", which previously appeared on his 1960 album \"Lonely and Blue\". This was Orbison's final album that was released for London Records as Decca let Orbison out of their contract on June 30, 1972.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The Memphis album was released on November 7, 1972.", "num_tokens": 16, "green_tokens": 7, "green_fraction": 0.4375, "z_score": -0.5, "p_value": 0.6914624612740131, "dedup_num_tokens": 16, "dedup_green_tokens": 7, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.4375, "dedup_z_score": -0.5, "dedup_p_value": 0.6914624612740131, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 74, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
