{"id": "dolly-12108", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhat ingredients do i need to make sour dough bread\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "You will need:\n\n- 2 cups flour\n- 1 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup salt\n- 1 egg\n- 1/4 cup vegetable oil\n- 1/4 cup milk (optional)\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Preheat oven to 425°F (218°C).\n\n2. In a mixing bowl, combine flour, sugar, and salt. Mix well.\n\n3. In another mixing bowl, combine the egg, vegetable oil, and milk (if using). Mix well.\n\n4. Pour the wet ingredients over the dry ingredients.\n\n5. Use a spoon to mix the dough until it's smooth and slightly sticky.\n\n6. Place the dough on a floured surface and knead it for about 30 seconds.\n\n7. Transfer the dough to a baking sheet and bake for about 25 minutes or until it's golden brown.\n\n8. Let the bread cool on the baking sheet for about 15 minutes before slicing.\n\n9. Serve hot!\n\nurn", "num_tokens": 206, "green_tokens": 105, "green_fraction": 0.5097087378640777, "z_score": 0.2786932057166471, "p_value": 0.3902401385347492, "dedup_num_tokens": 167, "dedup_green_tokens": 86, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5149700598802395, "dedup_z_score": 0.38691161626706844, "dedup_p_value": 0.34941082055702083, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 81, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
