{"id": "dolly-00105", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhat is the Maareech Advanced Torpedo Defence System (ATDS)?\n\n### Context:\nMaareech Advanced Torpedo Defence System (ATDS) is a torpedo detection and countermeasure system used by the Indian Navy. The system offers a complete solution to detect and locate an incoming torpedo and to apply countermeasures to protect naval platform against torpedo attack. It was developed as a joint project of the Naval Physical and Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL), Kochi and the Naval Science and Technological Laboratory (NSTL), Visakhapatnam. Bharat Electronics is manufacturing it India.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The Maareech Advanced Torpedo Defence System (ATDS) is a sophisticated system designed for detecting and responding to incoming torpedoes. It is a joint project involving the Naval Physical and Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL) in Kochi and the Naval Science and Technological Laboratory (NSTL) in Visakhapatnam. The ATDS system is designed to provide a comprehensive solution for detecting and protecting naval platforms against torpedo attacks. It is a joint project of the two institutions, with Bharat Electronics manufacturing the system.", "num_tokens": 105, "green_tokens": 54, "green_fraction": 0.5142857142857142, "z_score": 0.29277002188455997, "p_value": 0.3848489718906449, "dedup_num_tokens": 94, "dedup_green_tokens": 47, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5, "dedup_z_score": 0.0, "dedup_p_value": 0.5, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 133, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-00420", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nExtract the names of the cities and rank them in alphabetical order?\n\n### Context:\nThe United Kingdom is a constitutional monarchy and parliamentary democracy. Its capital and largest city is London, the capital of England, a global city and financial centre with a population of over 14 million people. Edinburgh, Cardiff and Belfast are the national capitals of Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland respectively.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The cities and their corresponding ranks in alphabetical order are:\nLondon - 7\nEdinburgh - 7\nCardiff - 7\nBelfast - 7", "num_tokens": 33, "green_tokens": 24, "green_fraction": 0.7272727272727273, "z_score": 2.6111648393354674, "p_value": 0.004511719409040167, "dedup_num_tokens": 25, "dedup_green_tokens": 18, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.72, "dedup_z_score": 2.2, "dedup_p_value": 0.01390344751349861, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 134, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-14313", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nGiven this paragraph about Mohamed Fourati, at what age was he appointed as hospital assistant?\n\n### Context:\nA year after getting his philosophy baccalaureate in his native town Sfax, Mohamed Fourati moved to Lille (France) to pursue his graduate education in the medical school of Lille. In order to validate his studies, he became an intern in the Farhat-Hachad Hospital of Sousse. Traveling between the two continents, he secured, in 1959, a medical doctorate at the medical school of Lille. He performed his military service, the following year, in the region of El Kef (in north-eastern Tunisia) and in Kébili (southern Tunisia). He continued to specialize in thoracic and cardiovascular surgery at the Saint-Joseph Hospital of Paris. He got assigned to the general surgery unit of doctors Saïd Mestiri and Zouhair Essafi at the Habib-Thameur Hospital in Tunis. In 1961, over the month of July, he worked as a surgeon in the battle of Bizerte, performing surgery on patients 20 hours a day for many days. He got appointed as hospital assistant in 1966, then earned the title of chief physician of the surgical ward in the Habib-Thameur Hospital in May 1968 and became, at the age of 35, the youngest chief physician in Tunisia. In November of the same year, he performed the first open-heart surgery, favored by a delegation of doctors of the IFTHD (led by Charles Hahn of the Cantonal hospital of Geneva (Switzerland) ).\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "Mohamed Fourati was appointed as hospital assistant in Tunisia in 1966. He received his doctorate in medicine at the medical school of Lille and then worked as a surgeon in the Habib-Thameur Hospital in Tunis. He was appointed as hospital assistant in May 1968 and became the youngest chief physician in Tunisia at the age of 35. He performed the first open-heart surgery on July 29th, 1966, and was the first chief physician in Tunisia to perform such surgery.", "num_tokens": 111, "green_tokens": 63, "green_fraction": 0.5675675675675675, "z_score": 1.4237369936287485, "p_value": 0.0772613103142331, "dedup_num_tokens": 91, "dedup_green_tokens": 51, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5604395604395604, "dedup_z_score": 1.1531133203941102, "dedup_p_value": 0.12443193746896106, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 135, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
