{"id": "dolly-02004", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhich TV Show is about a zip code in Beverly Hills?\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The TV show you are looking for is called \"Beverly Hills\" and it's a comedy series that follows a group of people living in the fictional city of Beverly Hills. It's set in the 1930s and features a lot of action and fun with a lot of comedy and quirky characters.", "num_tokens": 64, "green_tokens": 36, "green_fraction": 0.5625, "z_score": 1.0, "p_value": 0.15865525393145707, "dedup_num_tokens": 61, "dedup_green_tokens": 33, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5409836065573771, "dedup_z_score": 0.6401843996644799, "dedup_p_value": 0.261026361857644, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 142, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-02761", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhat is a Roth 401(k)?\n\n### Context:\nIn the United States, a 401(k) plan is an employer-sponsored, defined-contribution, personal pension (savings) account, as defined in subsection 401(k) of the U.S. Internal Revenue Code. Periodical employee contributions come directly out of their paychecks, and may be matched by the employer. This legal option is what makes 401(k) plans attractive to employees, and many employers offer this option to their (full-time) workers.\n\nThere are two types: traditional and Roth 401(k). For Roth accounts, contributions and withdrawals have no impact on income tax. For traditional accounts, contributions may be deducted from taxable income and withdrawals are added to taxable income. There are limits to contributions, rules governing withdrawals and possible penalties.\n\nThe benefit of the Roth account is from tax-free capital gains. The net benefit of the traditional account is the sum of (1) a possible bonus (or penalty) from withdrawals at tax rates lower (or higher) than at contribution, and (2) the impact on qualification for other income-tested programs from contributions and withdrawals reducing and adding to taxable income, minus the consequences of capital gains being taxed at regular income rates.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The Roth 401(k) is a tax-free account that allows employees to contribute and withdraw tax-free income at the employee's own discretion. It is a type of individual retirement plan, or IRA, that offers tax advantages over traditional 401(k) plans.", "num_tokens": 56, "green_tokens": 31, "green_fraction": 0.5535714285714286, "z_score": 0.8017837257372732, "p_value": 0.2113390370853177, "dedup_num_tokens": 49, "dedup_green_tokens": 27, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5510204081632653, "dedup_z_score": 0.7142857142857143, "dedup_p_value": 0.23752526202697655, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 143, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
