{"id": "dolly-10290", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhat was the united Arab republic?\n\n### Context:\nIn 1958, Egypt and Syria formed a sovereign union known as the United Arab Republic. The union was short-lived, ending in 1961 when Syria seceded, thus ending the union. During most of its existence, the United Arab Republic was also in a loose confederation with North Yemen (or the Mutawakkilite Kingdom of Yemen), known as the United Arab States. In 1959, the All-Palestine Government of the Gaza Strip, an Egyptian client state, was absorbed into the United Arab Republic under the pretext of Arab union, and was never restored. The Arab Socialist Union, a new nasserist state-party was founded in 1962.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The united Arab Republic was formed in 1958, and it was short-lived, ending in 1961 when Syria seceded. It was a loose confederation with North Yemen (or the Mutawakkilite Kingdom of Yemen), and in 1959, the All-Palestine Government of the Gaza Strip, an Egyptian client state, was absorbed into the united Arab Republic under the pretext of Arab union.", "num_tokens": 92, "green_tokens": 37, "green_fraction": 0.40217391304347827, "z_score": -1.876629726513673, "p_value": 0.9697155698986712, "dedup_num_tokens": 83, "dedup_green_tokens": 37, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.4457831325301205, "dedup_z_score": -0.9878783399072131, "dedup_p_value": 0.8383938826888461, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token