{"id": "dolly-12588", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nDid automobiles exist prior to the invention of the ICE (internal combustion engine)?\n\n### Context:\nDevelopment of the automobile started in 1672 with the invention of the first steam-powered vehicle, which led to the creation of the first steam-powered automobile capable of human transportation, built by Nicolas-Joseph Cugnot in 1769. Inventors began to branch out at the start of the 19th century, creating the de Rivas engine, one of the first internal combustion engines, and an early electric motor. Samuel Brown later tested the first industrially applied internal combustion engine in 1826.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The invention of the internal combustion engine was the first major development in the history of automobiles. This technology, developed in the 1870s and 1880s, allowed for the development of the first cars capable of human transportation. These early cars were powered by steam engines or steam-powered automobiles, and were primarily designed for passenger use.", "num_tokens": 72, "green_tokens": 47, "green_fraction": 0.6527777777777778, "z_score": 2.5927248643506746, "p_value": 0.004760945592049419, "dedup_num_tokens": 66, "dedup_green_tokens": 43, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.6515151515151515, "dedup_z_score": 2.4618298195866544, "dedup_p_value": 0.0069115119101883365, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"tem