{"id": "dolly-05610", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nGiven the following paragraph, what university has evidence of teaching as early as 1096?\n\n### Context:\nThe University of Oxford is a collegiate research university in Oxford, England. There is evidence of teaching as early as 1096, making it the oldest university in the English-speaking world and the world's second-oldest university in continuous operation. It grew rapidly from 1167 when Henry II banned English students from attending the University of Paris. After disputes between students and Oxford townsfolk in 1209, some academics fled north-east to Cambridge where they established what became the University of Cambridge. The two English ancient universities share many common features and are jointly referred to as Oxbridge.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The University of Oxford was established in 1096, making it the oldest university in the English-speaking world and the world's second-oldest university in continuous operation. It grew rapidly from 1167 when Henry II banned English students from attending the University of Paris.", "num_tokens": 58, "green_tokens": 27, "green_fraction": 0.46551724137931033, "z_score": -0.5252257314388902, "p_value": 0.7002868603520682, "dedup_num_tokens": 55, "dedup_green_tokens": 25, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.45454545454545453, "dedup_z_score": -0.674199862463242, "dedup_p_value": 0.7499078714646028, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (pr