{"id": "dolly-09344", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhy Bangalore climate is pleasant\n\n### Context:\nBangalore is situated in the southeast of the South Indian state of Karnataka. It is positioned at 12.97° N 77.56° E and covers an area of 2,190 square kilometres (850 sq mi). A landlocked city, Bangalore is located in the heart of the Mysore Plateau (a region of the larger Deccan Plateau) at an average elevation of 920 metres (3,020 ft). Bangalore district borders with Kolar and Chikkaballapur in the northeast, Tumkur in the northwest, and Mandya and Ramanagaram in the southeast.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "Bangalore's climate is pleasant because it is located in the southeast of the South Indian state of Karnataka, which is situated in the tropical rainforest climate zone. This region experiences a tropical rainforest climate, characterized by a warm, humid climate with high temperatures throughout the year and heavy rainfall throughout the year. As a result of this tropical climate, Bangalore experiences a tropical rainforest climate, characterized by a warm, humid climate with high temperatures throughout the year and heavy rainfall throughout the year.", "num_tokens": 97, "green_tokens": 54, "green_fraction": 0.5567010309278351, "z_score": 1.116880781646981, "p_value": 0.13202265142261135, "dedup_num_tokens": 64, "dedup_green_tokens": 34, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.53125, "dedup_z_score": 0.5, "dedup_p_value": 0.3085375387259869, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_thre