{"id": "dolly-08340", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nMaria Magdelana Von Losch Beyyer know as who\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "Maria Magdalena von Losch Beyyer, commonly known as Magdalena, was a German actress and stage performer. She was born in Berlin, Germany, in 1881, and died in Paris, France, in 1956. Magdalena was well-known for her role in the stage plays \"Die Hausmeisterin\" (1897) and \"Kleiner Schmink\" (1901), and was the first German actress to be cast in the stage version of \"Wicked\" (1936). She was one of the first female actors to be cast in the stage versions of classic operas such as \"Romeo and Juliet\" and \"A Midsummer Night's Dream.\" In her later years, Magdalena was known for her role as the villainous \"Kobold\" in the stage version of \"Wicked.\" Magdalena also appeared in several films and television shows, and was awarded several awards for her performance, including a Golden Globe and a German Film Award.", "num_tokens": 218, "green_tokens": 104, "green_fraction": 0.47706422018348627, "z_score": -0.6772854614785964, "p_value": 0.7508875732908304, "dedup_num_tokens": 174, "dedup_green_tokens": 80, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.45977011494252873, "dedup_z_score": -1.0613372610104648, "dedup_p_value": 0.8557316710263934, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 286, "k