{"id": "dolly-03696", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhat factors influence mental health issues in young people?\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "Certainly! Here's my response to the instruction:\n\n youngster mental health issues can be influenced by a number of factors, including genetics, environment, and personal experiences. Genetics can play a role in determining an individual's susceptibility to certain mental health issues. Environmental factors such as trauma, abuse, and poverty can also impact an individual's mental health. Personal experiences, such as loss, stress, and depression, can also contribute to mental health issues. Additionally, social support and relationships can impact an individual's mental health. It is essential to recognize the importance of addressing these factors and providing appropriate support and resources to help individuals in need.", "num_tokens": 125, "green_tokens": 66, "green_fraction": 0.528, "z_score": 0.6260990336999411, "p_value": 0.2656249929974241, "dedup_num_tokens": 106, "dedup_green_tokens": 58, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5471698113207547, "dedup_z_score": 0.9712858623572641, "dedup_p_value": 0.16570297347245727, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 321, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-07132", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nExtract the locations where McEwan lived as a child and list them using bullets.\n\n### Context:\nMcEwan was born in Aldershot, Hampshire, on 21 June 1948, the son of David McEwan and Rose Lilian Violet (née Moore). His father was a working-class Scotsman who had worked his way up through the army to the rank of major.\n\nMcEwan spent much of his childhood in East Asia (including Singapore), Germany, and north Africa (including Libya), where his father was posted. His family returned to England when he was 12 years old. He was educated at Woolverstone Hall School in Suffolk; the University of Sussex, where he received a degree in English literature in 1970; and the University of East Anglia, where he undertook a master's degree in literature (with the option to submit creative writing instead of a critical dissertation).\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "McEwan's childhood was marked by a mix of adventure and danger, with him spending much of his time in East Asia (including Singapore), Germany, and north Africa (including Libya). He was educated at Woolverstone Hall School and the University of Sussex, and later went to the University of East Anglia to undertake a master's degree in literature with the option to submit creative writing instead of a critical dissertation.", "num_tokens": 84, "green_tokens": 51, "green_fraction": 0.6071428571428571, "z_score": 1.9639610121239315, "p_value": 0.02476730671781337, "dedup_num_tokens": 80, "dedup_green_tokens": 48, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.6, "dedup_z_score": 1.78885438