{"id": "dolly-05761", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nBest Tea in the World\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The best tea in the world is Assam. It is a high-altitude tea that is known for its rich flavors and unique characteristics. It is made from the leaves of the Assam tea plant, and it is a staple ingredient in many traditional Assamese dishes.", "num_tokens": 55, "green_tokens": 38, "green_fraction": 0.6909090909090909, "z_score": 2.8316394223456167, "p_value": 0.002315501956331153, "dedup_num_tokens": 51, "dedup_green_tokens": 34, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.6666666666666666, "dedup_z_score": 2.3804761428476167, "dedup_p_value": 0.008645140296453134, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 333, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-01939", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nGiven this paragraph about the Mercury Seven. Who did not survive to reach retirement and what was the cause of their death?\n\n### Context:\nThe Mercury Seven were the group of seven astronauts selected to fly spacecraft for Project Mercury. They are also referred to as the Original Seven and Astronaut Group 1. Their names were publicly announced by NASA on April 9, 1959; these seven original American astronauts were Scott Carpenter, Gordon Cooper, John Glenn, Gus Grissom, Wally Schirra, Alan Shepard, and Deke Slayton. The Mercury Seven created a new profession in the United States, and established the image of the American astronaut for decades to come.\n\nAll of the Mercury Seven eventually flew in space. They piloted the six spaceflights of the Mercury program that had an astronaut on board from May 1961 to May 1963, and members of the group flew on all of the NASA human spaceflight programs of the 20th century – Mercury, Gemini, Apollo, and the Space Shuttle.\n\nShepard became the first American to enter space in 1961, and later walked on the Moon on Apollo 14 in 1971. Grissom flew the first crewed Gemini mission in 1965, but died in 1967 in the Apollo 1 fire; the others all survived past retirement from service. Schirra flew Apollo 7 in 1968, the first crewed Apollo mission, in Grissom's place. Slayton, grounded with an atrial fibrillation, ultimately flew on the Apollo–Soyuz Test Project in 1975. The first American in orbit in 1962, Glenn flew on the Space Shuttle Discovery in 1998 to become, at age 77, the oldest person to fly in space at the time. He was the last living member of the Mercury Seven when he died in 2016 at age 95.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The original seven astronauts who served as part of the Mercury Seven program include:\n1) Scott Carpenter\n2) Gordon Cooper\n3) John Glenn\n4) Gus Grissom\n5) Walter Schirra\n6) Alan Shepard\n7) Deke Slayton", "num_tokens": 56, "green_tokens": 24, "green_fraction": 0.42857142857142855, "z_score": -1.0690449676496976, "p_value": 0.8574752962986936, "dedup_num_tokens": 56, "dedup_green_tokens": 24, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.42857142857142855, "dedup_z_score": -1.0690449676496976, "dedup_p_value": 0.8574752962986936, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 334, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-05628", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nTell me if these are types of rock or types of fungi: sedimentary, yeasts, mildews, metamorphic, igneous, smuts, rusts, molds.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "Rock refers to the remains of plant life preserved in sedimentary rocks. It is made up of minerals that are deposited in layers by weathering or other processes. It is a natural substance that forms from rock fragments that have been dissolved, weathered, or eroded over time.\n\nFungi refers to the group of organisms that are characterized by a complex life cycle and a distinct nucleus. Fungi are multicellular organisms with a nucleus that contains their genetic material. They are found in various environments and are classified into two main groups: eukaryotic fungi and mycorrhizal fungi. Eukaryotic fungi are multicellular organisms with a nucleus that contains their genetic material, while mycorrhizal fungi are unicellular organisms that live in association with trees or plants. \n\nSedimentary rocks are formed from the remains of plant and animal life that have been deposited in sediment. They are made up of minerals that are deposited in layers by weathering or other processes. They are a natural substance that forms from rock fragments that have been dissolved, weathered, or eroded over time.\n\nMildews, metamorphic rocks, and smuts are all types of fungi. Mildews are unicellular organisms that live in association with trees or plants. They are characterized by a complex life cycle and a distinct nucleus. Metamorphic rocks are formed from the remains of rock fragments that have been weathered, eroded, or dissolved over time. Smuts are unicellular organisms that live in association with trees or plants. They are characterized by a complex life cycle and a distinct nucleus.", "num_tokens": 320, "green_tokens": 172, "green_fraction": 0.5375, "z_score": 1.3416407864998738, "p_value": 0.08985624743949992, "dedup_num_tokens": 178, "dedup_green_tokens": 96, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.5393258426966292, "dedup_z_score": 1.049344364594206, "dedup_p_value": 0.14700982712632116, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 335, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
