{"id": "dolly-01206", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nWhat is the top floor of the King's Building based on this article? What floor is found below that?\n\n### Context:\nThe King's Building is a Grade I listed building that forms part of the Strand Campus of King's College London in the United Kingdom. Originally named the College Building, the King's Building was designed by Sir Robert Smirke in the course of the College's foundation in 1829. As the founding building, it was built between 1829 and 1831 on land granted to King's College by the Government to complete the riverside frontage of Somerset House.\n\nThere are today a total of eight floors in the King's Building: Basement level, Ground level, Levels 1 to 4, Level 4U and Level 6. The King's Building houses a number of administrative departments (Estates & Facilities Offices, Admissions Office, Accommodation and Cashiers' Office), lecture theatres (most notably the Edmond J. Safra Lecture Theatre and Anatomy Lecture Theatre), the College Chapel, the Great Hall, various function rooms (Old Council Room, Committee Room, River Room, Somerset Room, St David's Room), study rooms and a catering outlet.\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "The top floor of the King's Building is located on the ground floor.", "num_tokens": 15, "green_tokens": 9, "green_fraction": 0.6, "z_score": 0.7745966692414834, "p_value": 0.21928901304049994, "dedup_num_tokens": 15, "dedup_green_tokens": 9, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.6, "dedup_z_score": 0.7745966692414834, "dedup_p_value": 0.21928901304049994, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 342, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
{"id": "dolly-09334", "model_label": "kgw_trained_student", "label": "kgw", "is_watermarked": true, "model_path": "/shared/wwx/EasyGAD/checkpoints/te_old_st_Qwen2.5-0.5B_gamma0.5_delta3/warmup/global_step_1813/actor/huggingface", "prompt": [{"content": "You are a helpful assistant.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request.\n\n### Instruction:\nGive me 5 facts about Singapore\n\n### Response:\n", "role": "user"}], "answer": "Singapore is a country located in Southeast Asia. It is known for its beautiful beaches, rich history, and vibrant culture. Here are five facts about Singapore:\n\n1. Singapore is known as the \"World City\" due to its thriving economy and vibrant culture.\n2. Singapore's capital, Singapore, is a beautiful city with a population of over 5 million people.\n3. Singapore's economy is diverse and includes manufacturing, tourism, and services.\n4. Singapore's cuisine is a blend of East and West, with a mix of Chinese, Malay, and Indian influences.\n5. Singapore's infrastructure is one of the most advanced in the region, with a high standard of living and a high standard of living.", "num_tokens": 142, "green_tokens": 87, "green_fraction": 0.6126760563380281, "z_score": 2.685380346549405, "p_value": 0.00362236549516564, "dedup_num_tokens": 121, "dedup_green_tokens": 75, "dedup_green_fraction": 0.6198347107438017, "dedup_z_score": 2.6363636363636362, "dedup_p_value": 0.0041899937205068325, "kgw": {"gamma": 0.5, "delta": 3.0, "hash_key": 15485863, "seeding": "simple_1 (hash_key * previous_token_id)", "detection_threshold_z": 4.0, "deduplication": "unique (previous_token_id, token_id) pairs"}, "generation": {"temperature": 0.7, "top_p": 0.9, "max_new_tokens": 1536, "max_prompt_tokens": 2048, "seed": 343, "kgw_enabled_during_generation": false}}
